  "note": "The four-consonant insect name has parallels at Ebla and Ugarit. The Phoenician evidence comes from a name on a gemstone of unknown provenance. The initial b in Arabic and Maltese differs from Hebrew p. The two Hebrew occurrences of the insect are distinct from the identically spelled personal name Parosh in Ezra and Nehemiah."
